            <ArticleTitle>Headache: a rare manifestation of Debakey type I aortic dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291.e5-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ajem.2013.10.022</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0735-6757(13)00693-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The most common manifestations of aortic dissection (AD) are severe chest pain and back pain. However, we experienced a rare case of type I aortic dissection with bilateral common carotid artery involvement, which presented with only a sudden thunderclap bifrontal headache.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
